<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: European Leisure yr pre-tax profit up 30pct.</title>
<headline>European Leisure yr pre-tax profit up 30pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		40.7		   vs 31.2</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    5.39		   vs 4.13</p>
<p> Turnover		   76.66		  vs 68.20</p>
<p> Operating profit	 9.46		   vs 8.80</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs 0.3 loss</p>
<p> Interest payable	 4.07		   vs 4.36</p>
<p> Tax			  nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Net taxed		  5.39		   vs 4.13</p>
<p>NOTE - European Leisure Plc said the results reflected the significant progress made by the company during the last year.</p>
<p>It said current trading was ahead of the same period last year and the board remained optimistic about the group's future trading prospects.</p>
<p>The directors were continuing to keep dividend policy under close review but were not recommending payment of a dividend for this year, the company said.</p>
<p>	  -- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
